{
  "kanji": "係",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 係\ntitle: connection; person in charge\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 人\nradicalNumber: 9\nonyomi: [ケイ]\nkunyomi: [かか.る, かかり, -がかり, かか.わる]\ndistractors: [休, 体, 作]\n---\n\n# 係 — connection; person in charge\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 人 (as 亻, no. 9) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n係 appears in [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい, a relationship or connection.\nAs the word 係 かかり, it can identify a duty or the person responsible for it.\nThese uses help connect involvement with having an assigned role, without making the words interchangeable.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the person on the left holding the thread-like lines on the right, keeping connections organized.\nThis is a visual learning story, not a verified historical analysis.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ケイ | on | [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい — relationship |\n| かかり | kun | 係 かかり — person in charge; duty |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい — relation; connection\n- 係 かかり — person in charge; assigned duty\n\n## Notes\n\n係 can stand as a noun: 係の人 (かかりのひと), \"the person in charge.\"\nIts 亻 is the left-side form of radical 人.\nCompare [休](休.md), [体](体.md), and [作](作.md): the shared person component is not enough to identify the character.\nPreserve the distinction between the on reading ケイ in 関係 and the independent word かかり.\n",
